  "worked_solution": "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$ to make the coefficient of the cubic term positive. This gives\n\n$$\n2{r}^{3}-12{r}^{2}-3r+18=0.\n$$\n\nWe then proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{r}^{3}-12{r}^{2}-3r+18 & = \\\\ (2{r}^{3}-12{r}^{2})+(-3r+18) & = \\\\ 2{r}^{2}(r-6)-3(r-6) & = \\\\ (2{r}^{2}-3)(r-6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(2{r}^{2}-3)(r-6)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(2{r}^{2}-3)$ equal to $0,$ we get $r=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(r-6)$ equal to $0,$ we get $r=6.$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $r=6,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}.$",
